### =============================================================
### Identity — HTTP test suite
### Covers GET /v1/me, its auth gate, and the proof that the old
### bootstrap routes are gone (phase 06, defect D8).
###
### Endpoints under test:
###   GET  /v1/me                          (auth: Bearer irk_*.*)
###
### Merchants and API keys are NOT managed over HTTP. Create them with
### the operator CLI from the repo root:
###
###   make irisctl ARGS="create-merchant --legal-name 'Acme' --document 12345678000100 --contact-email ops@acme.example.com"
###   make irisctl ARGS="issue-api-key --merchant-id <merchant id>"
###   make irisctl ARGS="revoke-api-key --id <api key id>"
###
### `issue-api-key` prints the secret once. Paste it into @api_key_token
### below; paste the secret of a key you revoked into @revoked_token.
###
### Token format: irk_<prefix>.<secret>
### Error format: application/problem+json (RFC 7807)
### =============================================================

### Variables
@base_url = http://localhost:8080
@api_key_token = irk_PASTE_ACTIVE_KEY_HERE
@revoked_token = irk_PASTE_REVOKED_KEY_HERE
@some_id = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### =============================================================
### 1. GET /v1/me with an active key
### =============================================================

### 1.1 GET /v1/me with the issued key (expect 200, returns merchant)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### =============================================================
### 2. GET /v1/me — auth gate surface
### Validates RequireAPIKey middleware behavior:
###   missing/malformed header → 401 missing_credentials
###   token doesn't decode or hash mismatch → 401 invalid_credentials
###   key was revoked → 403 revoked
### =============================================================

### 2.1 No Authorization header (expect 401 missing_credentials)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/me

### 2.2 Authorization without "Bearer " prefix (expect 401)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/me
Authorization: {{ api_key_token }}

### 2.3 Bearer with empty token (expect 401)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer

### 2.4 Bearer with garbage token — wrong format (expect 401 invalid_credentials)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token

### 2.5 Bearer with valid format but wrong secret (expect 401)
# Prefix shape ok, secret part forged — hash won't match.
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer irk_aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb

### 2.6 Bearer with unknown prefix (expect 401)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer irk_0000000000000000.0000000000000000000000000000000000

### 2.7 Bearer using a revoked key (expect 403 revoked)
# Revoke first: make irisctl ARGS="revoke-api-key --id <api key id>"
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{ revoked_token }}

### =============================================================
### 3. METHOD ERRORS
### =============================================================

### 3.1 OPTIONS on a protected route (expect 200/204 — chi default OPTIONS)
OPTIONS {{ base_url }}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 3.2 HEAD on /v1/me (expect 200 with no body — auth still enforced)
HEAD {{ base_url }}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 3.3 HEAD on /v1/me without auth (expect 401)
HEAD {{ base_url }}/v1/me

### 3.4 PUT on /v1/me (expect 405 — only GET is routed)
PUT {{ base_url }}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### =============================================================
### 4. REMOVED BOOTSTRAP ROUTES (AC6, defect D8)
### These paths no longer exist. Every request below expects 404
### (or 405) and must not create or revoke anything.
### =============================================================

### 4.1 POST /v1/merchants (expect 404)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/merchants
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "legal_name": "Acme Pagamentos LTDA",
    "document": "12345678000100",
    "contact_email": "ops@acme.example.com"
}

### 4.2 POST /v1/api-keys (expect 404)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/api-keys
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "merchant_id": "{{ some_id }}"
}

### 4.3 POST /v1/api-keys/{id}/revoke (expect 404)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/api-keys/{{ some_id }}/revoke

### 4.4 GET /v1/merchants (expect 404)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/merchants
